WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.420
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Sarah. Welcome to Online Proficiency.

2
00:00:05.720 --> 00:00:08.967
Hi! I'm Rithy. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.267 --> 00:00:18.699
Unit fifty-eight: The Future of Language Learning. In this unit, you will paraphrase and summarise views on how languages will be learned.

4
00:00:19.683 --> 00:00:21.218
language acquisition.

5
00:00:21.918 --> 00:00:27.401
language acquisition means the natural process of learning a language, especially through exposure.

6
00:00:27.701 --> 00:00:32.243
Children's language acquisition happens through play and conversation.

7
00:00:32.943 --> 00:00:36.431
Your turn. Say: language acquisition.

8
00:00:39.131 --> 00:00:40.725
language acquisition.

9
00:00:41.717 --> 00:00:42.938
immersion learning.

10
00:00:43.638 --> 00:00:47.774
immersion learning means learning by being surrounded by the target language.

11
00:00:48.074 --> 00:00:51.571
Immersion learning in an English camp boosted their confidence.

12
00:00:52.271 --> 00:00:55.597
Your turn. Say: immersion learning.

13
00:00:58.297 --> 00:00:59.739
immersion learning.

14
00:01:00.750 --> 00:01:02.541
AI language partner.

15
00:01:03.241 --> 00:01:09.547
AI language partner means an artificial intelligence tool that practises conversation with learners.

16
00:01:09.847 --> 00:01:13.751
An AI language partner is available at midnight before an exam.

17
00:01:14.451 --> 00:01:18.613
Your turn. Say: AI language partner.

18
00:01:21.313 --> 00:01:23.730
AI language partner.

19
00:01:24.717 --> 00:01:26.066
translanguaging.

20
00:01:26.766 --> 00:01:33.642
translanguaging means using all of one's languages together to learn and communicate.

21
00:01:33.942 --> 00:01:38.693
Translanguaging lets students explain ideas in Khmer and English.

22
00:01:39.393 --> 00:01:43.009
Your turn. Say: translanguaging.

23
00:01:45.709 --> 00:01:47.058
translanguaging.

24
00:01:48.050 --> 00:01:49.341
plurilingualism.

25
00:01:50.041 --> 00:01:54.920
plurilingualism means an individual's ability to use several languages flexibly.

26
00:01:55.220 --> 00:01:59.658
Plurilingualism is normal in much of Asia and Africa.

27
00:02:00.358 --> 00:02:03.684
Your turn. Say: plurilingualism.

28
00:02:06.384 --> 00:02:07.710
plurilingualism.

29
00:02:08.717 --> 00:02:10.438
communicative competence.

30
00:02:11.138 --> 00:02:17.421
communicative competence means the ability to use language appropriately in real situations.

31
00:02:17.721 --> 00:02:21.950
Grammar knowledge alone does not guarantee communicative competence.

32
00:02:22.650 --> 00:02:26.173
Your turn. Say: communicative competence.

33
00:02:28.873 --> 00:02:30.582
communicative competence.

34
00:02:31.583 --> 00:02:32.991
learner autonomy.

35
00:02:33.691 --> 00:02:38.245
learner autonomy means learners taking responsibility for their own learning.

36
00:02:38.545 --> 00:02:42.518
Learner autonomy grows when students set their own goals.

37
00:02:43.218 --> 00:02:46.625
Your turn. Say: learner autonomy.

38
00:02:49.325 --> 00:02:50.732
learner autonomy.

39
00:02:51.717 --> 00:02:53.635
critical language awareness.

40
00:02:54.335 --> 00:02:59.922
critical language awareness means understanding how language reflects power and shapes opinions.

41
00:03:00.222 --> 00:03:03.824
Critical language awareness helps readers spot manipulation.

42
00:03:04.524 --> 00:03:08.523
Your turn. Say: critical language awareness.

43
00:03:11.223 --> 00:03:13.129
critical language awareness.

44
00:03:14.117 --> 00:03:16.325
Now let's listen to a conversation.

45
00:03:16.625 --> 00:03:21.353
Rithy, will AI make language teachers unnecessary?

46
00:03:22.650 --> 00:03:27.322
To put it another way: will machines replace human connection? I doubt it.

47
00:03:28.617 --> 00:03:31.626
Yet an AI language partner never gets tired.

48
00:03:32.917 --> 00:03:38.309
True. In short, AI is a tireless practice tool, not a teacher.

49
00:03:39.617 --> 00:03:41.059
What else will change?

50
00:03:42.350 --> 00:03:47.624
Roughly speaking, schools will value plurilingualism rather than a single 'correct' language.

51
00:03:48.917 --> 00:03:51.230
Summarise your view in one sentence.

52
00:03:52.517 --> 00:03:58.603
Essentially, technology will support learner autonomy, but people will still inspire learning.

53
00:03:59.917 --> 00:04:04.436
Grammar focus: Paraphrase and summary (advanced).

54
00:04:04.736 --> 00:04:07.722
Paraphrase and summary show mastery.

55
00:04:08.022 --> 00:04:16.572
To put it another way: will machines replace human connection? In short, AI is a practice tool, not a teacher.

56
00:04:16.872 --> 00:04:19.859
Essentially, people will still inspire learning.

57
00:04:20.159 --> 00:04:26.953
When summarising, cut examples and repetition, keep the main claim and reason, and use your own words.

58
00:04:27.950 --> 00:04:31.810
Now read and listen. Learning Languages in the Age of AI.

59
00:04:32.110 --> 00:04:36.327
Language learning is changing faster than at any time in history.

60
00:04:37.617 --> 00:04:43.378
Research on language acquisition shows that meaningful exposure and interaction are essential.

61
00:04:44.683 --> 00:04:52.511
Traditionally, immersion learning required travel abroad; now, an AI language partner can simulate conversation at home.

62
00:04:53.817 --> 00:05:01.981
At the same time, teachers increasingly recognise translanguaging, allowing learners to use their first language as a resource.

63
00:05:03.283 --> 00:05:10.786
The goal is no longer native-speaker perfection but plurilingualism and communicative competence.

64
00:05:12.083 --> 00:05:18.146
Learner autonomy has become crucial, as students must choose and manage countless digital tools.

65
00:05:19.450 --> 00:05:26.244
Critical language awareness also matters, since AI-generated text can be persuasive yet inaccurate.

66
00:05:27.550 --> 00:05:36.109
In short, technology will transform how we learn languages, but human motivation and connection will remain at the heart of learning.

67
00:05:37.417 --> 00:05:40.301
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

68
00:05:40.601 --> 00:05:44.145
Using all of one's languages together to learn is blank.

69
00:05:44.445 --> 00:05:50.211
A, translanguaging. B, immersion learning. C, language acquisition.

70
00:05:54.217 --> 00:05:57.133
The answer is A: translanguaging.

71
00:05:58.650 --> 00:06:01.613
Which phrase introduces a reformulation?

72
00:06:01.913 --> 00:06:06.646
A, To put it another way. B, In addition. C, However.

73
00:06:10.650 --> 00:06:13.451
The answer is A: To put it another way.

74
00:06:14.950 --> 00:06:16.636
A good summary should blank.

75
00:06:16.936 --> 00:06:24.607
A, keep the main claim in your own words. B, copy every sentence. C, add new examples.

76
00:06:28.617 --> 00:06:32.555
The answer is A: keep the main claim in your own words.

77
00:06:34.050 --> 00:06:37.605
Learners taking responsibility for their own learning is blank.

78
00:06:37.905 --> 00:06:44.020
A, learner autonomy. B, plurilingualism. C, communicative competence.

79
00:06:48.017 --> 00:06:50.910
The answer is A: learner autonomy.

80
00:06:52.417 --> 00:06:55.984
According to the text, what is the goal no longer?

81
00:06:56.284 --> 00:07:03.234
A, native-speaker perfection. B, communicative competence. C, plurilingualism.

82
00:07:07.250 --> 00:07:10.585
The answer is A: native-speaker perfection.

83
00:07:12.083 --> 00:07:17.522
Now it's your turn. Part one: How will people learn English in twenty years?

84
00:07:22.822 --> 00:07:29.396
Part two: Paraphrase one idea from the reading, then summarise your own view in one sentence.

85
00:07:35.696 --> 00:07:49.810
To put the reading's idea another way, machines will give us endless practice. However, motivation comes from people. Essentially, the best learners will combine AI tools, real conversation and their own goals.

86
00:07:50.110 --> 00:07:52.527
That is a well-argued answer!

87
00:07:53.517 --> 00:07:59.222
Great work today! You learned eight new words and paraphrase and summary (advanced).

88
00:07:59.522 --> 00:08:04.125
Today's value is pride in learning. Be proud of what you learned.

89
00:08:04.425 --> 00:08:07.333
See you in Unit fifty-nine. Goodbye!

90
00:08:07.633 --> 00:08:09.902
Thank you, Ms. Sarah! Bye, everyone!

